/ One bar between the arrows: the live view, the period and today. The
  segments keep their width whatever they show: a label in bold or the next
  period would move the row on each change. The period cuts a longer name
  short.

  optimistic-nav swaps the class lists of the segments, so all of them are
  children of one nav, each in its column, and the bar lies behind them.
nav.relative.grid.items-stretch.text-sm.font-medium[
  class='grid-cols-[1.25rem_1fr_2.5fr_1fr_1.25rem]'
  aria-label=t('.label')
  data-controller='optimistic-nav'
  data-optimistic-nav-slide-value='true'
  data-action=OptimisticNav::ACTIONS
]
  span class="#{BAR_CLASSES} col-span-3 col-start-2"

  = arrow(:prev, arrows[:prev], column: 1)

  = segment(live, column: 2)

  / The chevron says that a tap opens the choice of periods, so it shows on
    the current period alone. Elsewhere it keeps its room, so the name does
    not move when the period becomes the current one.
  = link_to period_href, **period_options do
    span.truncate = period[:name]
    = icon 'chevron-down', class: ['ml-1 w-3 shrink-0 text-xs', ('invisible' unless period[:current])]

  = segment(today, column: 4)

  = arrow(:next, arrows[:next], column: 5)
